                            <comment id="497516" author="JIRAUSER19474" created="Wed, 8 Jul 2026 21:18:11 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Code Analysis&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;In `lustre/ldlm/ldlm_flock.c`, the lock split code path:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;if (new2 == NULL) {&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&#160; &#160; unlock_res_and_lock(req); &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; // Release lock for allocation&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&#160; &#160; new2 = ldlm_lock_create(...); &#160; &#160; &#160; // May fail with -ENOMEM&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&#160; &#160; lock_res_and_lock(req); &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; // Re-acquire lock&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&#160; &#160; if (IS_ERR(new2)) &lt;/p&gt;
{

&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; ldlm_flock_destroy(req, lock-&amp;gt;l_granted_mode, *flags);

&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; *err = PTR_ERR(new2);

&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; RETURN(LDLM_ITER_STOP); &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; // BUG: Returns with lock held!

&#160; &#160; }

&lt;p&gt;&#160; &#160; goto reprocess;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;}&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This occurs when:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;1. A process holds a byte-range flock (e.g., bytes 0-999)&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;2. It unlocks a middle portion (e.g., bytes 100-199)&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;3. Server needs to split the lock into two separate locks&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;4. `ldlm_lock_create()` fails due to memory pressure (-ENOMEM)&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;5. Error path returns without releasing the resource lock&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="497517" author="gerrit" created="Wed, 8 Jul 2026 21:18:56 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&quot;Vandana Rungta &amp;lt;vrungta@amazon.com&amp;gt;&quot; uploaded a new patch: &lt;a href=&quot;https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/67131&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/67131&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
Subject: &lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20463&quot; title=&quot;ldlm: fix missing unlock_res_and_lock() in ldlm_process_flock_lock() error path&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;LU-20463&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-20463&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; ldlm: fix missing unlock in flock error path&lt;br/&gt;
